{
  "_what": "The Bodymind Booth's choices: every way a bodymind can be drawn, in the order the booth asks, and the words each choice is said in. tools/make-bodymind.py builds the booth's controls out of this file, writes the keys into avatar.js (which draws them) and into netlify/cb/lib.mjs (which checks every avatar kept against them), and refuses rather than guesses; see its docstring. The drawings are in avatar.js, keyed by the names here.",
  "_brief": "Ryan, 2026-10-14, from a proposal written after somebody in our community said they hoped for characters to dress one day: a bodymind builder of its own, dressed at the Dopamine Dress-Up Den and any shop that styles a character later, avatars kept in your Profile, one worn on the CB at a time and swapped at will, shown beside your name on Who's online, and sent as stickers. Ryan's calls the same day: the Dress-Up Den stays body-free and the bodies are drawn here, in a room of their own; avatars are the second thing the street keeps under a person; and only a claimed username wears one on the CB.",
  "_no_first_body": "NO BODY COMES FIRST. The booth opens on a bodymind drawn at random from the shape, skin, face and hair choices, and Start again draws another, so there is no body the booth starts from and nothing is called normal, average, default or standard. The page ships with nothing checked, which is what a page with scripts off shows: the choices, as a list.",
  "_aids": "WHAT YOU ALWAYS HAVE WITH YOU IS PART OF YOU HERE, NOT CLOTHES. Mobility aids, hearing aids, glasses and the rest are chosen in the booth and never sold in a shop, and nothing put on at the Dress-Up Den takes one off. A cane, crutches and a walker are for a bodymind on its feet; a chair has its own way of getting about, and the booth says so rather than drawing a cane leaning on nothing.",
  "_skin": "Ten tones of skin by how light or deep they are, named by number rather than by a word, because every word for a skin tone has been used against somebody; and four colours nobody is born in, on purpose, for anybody whose bodymind is not that kind of thing.",
  "_words": "Nothing here describes a body for somebody else. The booth reads your own choices back to you while you build, because a choice you cannot hear is not a choice; nowhere else says them. On the CB a drawing is silent to a screen reader unless its owner writes what it shows, in their own words.",
